sn35.31:1.18 | S: They don’t conceive anything to be the pleasant, painful, or neutral feeling that arises dependent on mind contact. They don’t conceive it in that, they don’t conceive it as that, and they don’t conceive that ‘that is mine.’ | T: and as to whatever feeling arises with mind-contact as condition … he does not conceive that, does not conceive in that, does not conceive from that, does not conceive, ‘That is mine.’
sn35.31:1.19 | S: For whatever you conceive it to be, whatever you conceive it in, whatever you conceive it as, and whatever you conceive to be ‘mine’: that becomes something else. | T: For, bhikkhus, whatever one conceives, whatever one conceives in, whatever one conceives from, whatever one conceives as ‘mine’—that is otherwise.
sn35.31:1.20 | S: The world is attached to being, taking pleasure only in being, yet it becomes something else. | T: The world, becoming otherwise, attached to becoming, seeks delight only in becoming.
sn35.31:1.21 | S: As far as the aggregates, elements, and sense fields extend, they don’t conceive anything to be that, they don’t conceive it in that, they don’t conceive it as that, and they don’t conceive that ‘that is mine.’ | T: “Whatever, bhikkhus, is the extent of the aggregates, the elements, and the sense bases, he does not conceive that, does not conceive in that, does not conceive from that, does not conceive, ‘That is mine.’
sn35.31:1.22 | S: Not conceiving, they don’t grasp at anything in the world. | T: “Since he does not conceive anything thus, he does not cling to anything in the world.
sn35.31:1.23 | S: Not grasping, they’re not anxious. Not being anxious, they personally become extinguished. | T: Not clinging, he is not agitated. Being unagitated, he personally attains Nibbāna.
sn35.31:1.24 | S: They understand: ‘Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place.’ | T: He understands: ‘Destroyed is birth, the holy life has been lived, what had to be done has been done, there is no more for this state of being.’
sn35.31:1.25 | S: This is the practice that’s conducive to uprooting all conceiving.” | T: “This, bhikkhus, is the way that is suitable for uprooting all conceivings.”
