## sn35.71
sn35.71:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, anyone who doesn’t truly understand the six fields of contact’s origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape | T: “Bhikkhus, if a bhikkhu does not understand as they really are the origin and the passing away, the gratification, the danger, and the escape, in the case of these six bases for contact,
sn35.71:1.2 | S: has not completed the spiritual journey and is far from this teaching and training.” | T: then he has not lived the holy life; he is far away from this Dhamma and Discipline.”
sn35.71:2.1 | S: When he said this, one of the mendicants said to the Buddha, | T: When this was said, a certain bhikkhu said to the Blessed One:
sn35.71:2.2 | S: “Here, sir, I’m discouraged. | T: “Here, venerable sir, I am lost,
sn35.71:2.3 | S: For I don’t truly understand the six fields of contact’s origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape.” | T: for I do not understand as they really are the origin and the passing away, the gratification, the danger, and the escape, in the case of these six bases for contact.”
